# Review routing, not enforcement.
#
# Everything is owned by the maintainer, so a pull request from anyone else
# requests a review automatically instead of sitting unnoticed. Review is
# enforced by branch protection on main, which requires an approving review and
# a green CI run before a merge is possible.
#
# `require_code_owner_reviews` is deliberately left off in branch protection:
# GitHub does not let an author approve their own pull request, so requiring a
# code-owner review would make the maintainer unable to merge their own work.

